## Problem

Making one book-summary video takes a lot of pieces: a script split into narration chunks, dozens of scene prompts, a cover, a title and caption, and a set of vertical reels. They used to live in a long AI chat, a pile of folders and a spreadsheet. Nothing showed what was done or what was left. Nobody knew what the audio would cost until the credits were spent.

## What it does

A workspace where the whole production kit for a video lives in one project. The full app sits behind a login, and a public version with simulated AI and audio lets anyone click through it.

1. **Get the package.** Run the AI Director inside the app, or paste in a conversation from Gemini. Either way, it is split into audio chunks, scenes, reels, covers and publishing text.
2. **Generate the narration.** One audio file per chunk through ElevenLabs. You see a credit and cost estimate before anything is spent. Save to a folder or download a ZIP.
3. **Work the visual board.** Every scene has its image prompt, plus a video prompt where it needs one, with copy buttons. Upload each finished image or video to the slot on its card. Filters show what is left to do.
4. **Finish the cover and SEO.** The YouTube cover prompt, headline, title and caption sit in one place.
5. **Build the reels.** A vertical (9:16) kit for each reel, with its own audio, board, cover and captions.
6. **Download everything.** One click collects all the files.

## The AI Director

The director works in 6 stages: architecture, script chapters, 16:9 scenes, animations and audio chunks, thumbnail and caption, and reels and covers. Each stage can use a different Gemini model, so light steps can run on a cheaper model than heavy ones. You see the cost of every turn, plus an estimate for the full run before it starts. The run can pause after each stage so a person can check it.

## One Setup page

Setup is the one place for the ElevenLabs and Gemini keys, which stay in the browser. It also lets you pick a Gemini model for each stage: cheap models do the bulk work, and the strongest model is kept for architecture and script. You can edit the credit and token rates, and every cost estimate in the app uses them.

## Built for a team's daily use

- **Safe sign-in.** The first run sets a password and gives you a recovery key.
- **Save without overwriting.** If the same project was changed somewhere else, the Save bar tells you instead of overwriting that work.
- **Uploads on every card.** Files are stored on Cloudflare R2. Bulk upload matches files to cards by name, like `scene_04.mp4` or `R01-cover.png`.
- **Progress everywhere.** Each tab shows how much is done, and a Next bar points to the next step.

## Outcome

A working tool covering the whole path from AI conversation to a finished upload kit, with 335 automated tests and a Playwright browser suite behind it. The public version uses a test book with simulated audio and director runs, so it shows the workflow rather than AI output or costs.

## Stack

Cloudflare Workers with D1 for project data and R2 for uploaded files, and a vanilla JavaScript front end with no framework. Gemini runs the director, and ElevenLabs makes the audio. An offline mode replaces both with simulated runs and placeholder tones, so it needs no keys and your files stay in your browser.
